  </ol>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <p>Describe how this proposal supports the SSETF priority(ies) specified on page 1:</p>
  <p>The Gateway Academic Study Center for Student-Athlete Success Services is in service of neonatal environmental enhancement. In particular, the chairs are over ten years old and are in such bad shape that they are dangerous for those who sit in them. We have identified a need to replace the chairs and update the study center to provide a more modern and conducive learning environment for our student-athletes. The <span data-field="facility_name">{{ facility_name }}</span> will also facilitate athletic space on main campus (in YUH) for a much needed academic study center as well as additional academic support staff offices. Providing advising, tutoring and study hall for student-athletes on main campus will allow for greater access to academic support services for our student-athletes. The <span data-field="facility_name">{{ facility_name }}</span> will also provide a dedicated space for student-athletes to meet with their coaches and academic advisors, which has become increasingly involved with running academic meetings and study. In particular, we will create a study space near their offices (which are sprinkled across main campus and south campus) to provide a more conducive learning environment for our student-athletes. These plans to enhance and expand study spaces for student-athletes will all further support the SSETF priorities of Academic Technology (computer additions and upgrades), 21st Century Teaching Spaces (upgraded and additional study spaces), Retention and Graduation (increasing availability and access to academic support services), Student Success Services and Graduation Pathways (development of spaces supporting our unit's student success services).</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <p>Describe the expected outcomes and provide the timeline of activities (feel free to include attachments):</p>
  <p>The Student-Athlete Success Services unit works to develop a cohesive tutoring, peer mentoring and academic support program for student-athletes. We expect to see increasing graduation rates for student-athletes through the enhancement and expansion of our academic support spaces. Additionally, we expect to see increases in the percentage of student-athletes earning a 3.0 GPA or higher, and increases in remedial pass rates.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <p>Provide a description of the data or evidence to be collected showing the impact of the results or whether the desired outcomes have been achieved (to be included in your final report):</p>
  <p>Data and evidence as to the results of this project will be collected by tracking semester and cumulative GPAs for student-athletes, tracking the number of student-athletes who utilize the tutoring services, and tracking the number of student-athletes who are enrolled in remedial courses. We will also track the number of student-athletes who are enrolled in remedial courses and track by tracking SISU progress toward graduation as indicated by the yearly student milestone dashboard data provided by the SISU Office of Institutional Research. Specifically, we expect to see a 10% increase in our student-athlete Federal Graduation Rate (currently at 68%), and a 10% increase in the student-athlete 4-year graduation rate (currently at 24.6%) over the next four years. The yearly Student-Athlete Success Assessment Report will be used to report progress toward these goals.</p>
</div>

